      "content": "# BCA Study App\n\nThis repository is a scaffold for the BCA Study App: a cross-platform PWA + native wrapper-ready app that provides per-university syllabus sectors (2026 and future years), an \"Important\" sector, automatic update pipeline, and offline-first behavior without requiring paid LLM APIs.\n\nKey decisions for this initial scaffold\n- No paid API required. The app uses a local/self-hosted LLM endpoint when available (env var LOCAL_LLM_URL). If none is configured the server returns a safe mocked response so the app works for development and publishing.\n- Public repo: gooner-collab/bca\n- Target platforms: Web PWA (installable), Android (TWA/Capacitor), iOS (Capacitor), Windows (Electron) — packaging instructions included.\n\nWhat’s in this first commit\n- backend/: Express server with auth skeleton, syllabus endpoints, solver proxy (local-model-first, mocked fallback), and scheduler stub for auto-updates.\n- frontend/: React PWA skeleton with per-university sector UI, login/register placeholders, solver UI, and Important sector view.\n- README with run & build instructions and notes about self-hosted LLMs and Play Store/App Store packaging.\n\nNext steps\n1. I will start building ingestion scripts to collect university syllabi (UGC list) and add parser templates for major Indian universities.\n2. Add stronger auth persistence (Postgres or SQLite), PGVector/FAISS embedding hooks, and worker processes for canonical answer generation using a local LLM server.\n3. Prepare TWA/Capacitor packaging for Play Store and build scripts for App Store / Microsoft Store.\n\nTo run locally (quick)\n1. Backend: cd backend && npm install && LOCAL_LLM_URL=http://localhost:5000 npm start\n2. Frontend: cd frontend && npm install && npm start\n\nLicense: MIT\n",
      "path": "README.md"
    },
